      "text": [
        "5837 - وَ قَالَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : \"إِنِّي لَأَرْحَمُ ثَلاَثَةً وَ حَقٌّ لَهُمْ أَنْ يُرْحَمُوا عَزِيزٌ أَصَابَتْهُ مَذَلَّةٌ بَعْدَ اَلْعِزِّ وَ غَنِيٌّ أَصَابَتْهُ حَاجَةٌ بَعْدَ اَلْغِنَى وَ عَالِمٌ يَسْتَخِفُّ بِهِ أَهْلُهُ وَ اَلْجَهَلَةُ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5837 - Abu Abdullah Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as), said:\n\"Indeed, I feel mercy for three people, and it is their right to be shown mercy:\nA noble person who has been humiliated after his honor,\nA wealthy person who has fallen into poverty after wealth,\nAnd a scholar who is belittled by his own people and the ignorant.\""
        ]
      }
